{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 35, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the sunlight oddly vibrant, almost *too* bright. He sat up in bed, the floral pattern of the duvet feeling unnervingly…pixelated. The room wasn't quite right. The furniture was too perfectly arranged, the colors a little too saturated. He glanced at his hands – smooth, flawless, lacking the usual imperfections of age and wear. A notification popped into his vision, a translucent window overlaid on reality: \"Welcome, Arthur! You are now in Aethelgard: Realm of Heroes. Level 1 achieved!\" Panic clawed at his throat. He scrambled out of bed, nearly tripping over a suspiciously blocky rug. The world seemed to hum with an underlying code, a faint digital thrumming beneath the sounds of birdsong. He reached for a mirror and saw not his own tired reflection, but a strikingly handsome man with impossibly sculpted features and eyes that seemed to glow with an inner light.\n\n***\n\nA gentle chime announced a quest update. \"Speak with Elder Rowan in Oakhaven village to begin your journey!\" another notification flashed. Oakhaven? Elder Rowan? It was all too much. Arthur felt a surge of disbelief, then a creeping sense of dread. He walked towards the door, each step feeling strangely predetermined. As he opened it, the world shifted subtly, the familiar suburban street transforming into a quaint village square filled with people who seemed…programmed. Their conversations were repetitive, their expressions predictable. A woman selling apples repeated the same greeting for the tenth time, her smile fixed and unnervingly wide. He was trapped. He was a character in a game, a pawn in someone else's digital world, and the only question was: could he find a way to break free?\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.32705190777778625}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0002044230350293219}